('6c05779d-7b87-5c1e-82d3-8b05ced23a2b'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The infective stage of hookworm is:', '["Adult worm","Rhabditiform larva","Filariform larva","Cyst","Egg"]'::jsonb, 'Filariform larva', 'Filariform larvae penetrate human skin, the infective stage of hookworms.'),
('4fa21d93-0150-5650-a78f-7d67f750fc66'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Strongyloides stercoralis is unique among nematodes because:', '["It causes the most severe infection","It can cause autoinfection","It requires an intermediate host","It is the smallest","It is blood-borne"]'::jsonb, 'It can cause autoinfection', 'Strongyloides can autoinfect, leading to persistent infection and hyperinfection in immunocompromised.'),
('ec0f950e-270b-5804-baa1-60ca03476bf3'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which nematode causes ''ground itch''?', '["Strongyloides","Trichuris","Ascaris","Enterobius","Hookworm"]'::jsonb, 'Hookworm', 'Hookworm filariform larvae cause ground itch (pruritic papular rash) at skin penetration site.'),
('ae3cdeba-0cd1-51b1-97e5-63e23745cced'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Enterobius vermicularis infection presents with:', '["Abdominal pain","Diarrhea","Nocturnal perianal pruritus","Fever","Weight loss"]'::jsonb, 'Nocturnal perianal pruritus', 'Pinworm (E. vermicularis) causes intense perianal itching, especially at night.'),
('498883b6-c6ae-514a-9208-680f07fd961c'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The scotch tape test is used to diagnose:', '["Ascariasis","Enterobiasis","Hookworm infection","Taeniasis","Trichuriasis"]'::jsonb, 'Enterobiasis', 'The cellophane (scotch) tape test detects E. vermicularis eggs in the perianal region.'),
('9bfff8d7-3fb2-55d2-8cd6-81d62abf28f3'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Trichuris trichiura (whipworm) causes:', '["Liver abscess","Rectal prolapse in heavy infections","Brain cysts","Hematuria","Pulmonary eosinophilia"]'::jsonb, 'Rectal prolapse in heavy infections', 'Heavy Trichuris infection can cause rectal prolapse, especially in children.'),
('601b3e12-b315-534b-ab17-45867e20de63'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Wuchereria bancrofti causes:', '["Lymphatic filariasis","Onchocerciasis","Loiasis","Dracunculiasis","Schistosomiasis"]'::jsonb, 'Lymphatic filariasis', 'W. bancrofti causes lymphatic filariasis with lymphedema and elephantiasis of limbs/genitalia.'),
('f0eb7dcb-6306-57c1-b01e-5762ed2c95b7'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The vector for Wuchereria bancrofti is:', '["Anopheles and Culex mosquitoes","Reduviid bug","Tsetse fly","Black fly","Sandfly"]'::jsonb, 'Anopheles and Culex mosquitoes', 'W. bancrofti is transmitted by Culex (urban) and Anopheles (rural) mosquitoes.'),
('aff972e7-d0ed-5f9a-a02b-6701e543b17f'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'bancrofti is diagnostic in blood?', '["Adult worm","Cyst","Microfilaria","Larva","Egg"]'::jsonb, 'Microfilaria', 'Microfilariae are detected in blood films, showing nocturnal periodicity.'),
('c74b6cc0-0a95-5663-81d3-6ad51013dbbc'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The drug of choice for lymphatic filariasis is:', '["Metronidazole","Ivermectin","Albendazole","Praziquantel","Diethylcarbamazine"]'::jsonb, 'Diethylcarbamazine', 'DEC is the drug of choice for lymphatic filariasis. Ivermectin is used for onchocerciasis.'),
('3c6b6a61-4a1e-5269-a51a-f1d8659a1d3f'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Leishmania tropica causes:', '["Mucocutaneous leishmaniasis","Visceral leishmaniasis","Post-kala-azar dermal leishmaniasis","Cutaneous leishmaniasis","Chagas disease"]'::jsonb, 'Cutaneous leishmaniasis', 'L. tropica causes cutaneous leishmaniasis (oriental sore), self-healing skin ulcers.'),
('8f90b15c-f5b6-5e3e-97dc-cf9466f42975'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The vector for leishmaniasis is:', '["Anopheles mosquito","Sandfly","Tsetse fly","Blackfly","Reduviid bug"]'::jsonb, 'Sandfly', 'Leishmania is transmitted by the bite of infected female sandflies (Phlebotomus in Old World).'),
('146dc785-558c-5f21-b9f8-be2d6912f329'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Visceral leishmaniasis presents with:', '["Fever, splenomegaly, pancytopenia","Skin ulcers","Mucosal lesions","Lymphadenopathy alone","Hematuria"]'::jsonb, 'Fever, splenomegaly, pancytopenia', 'Kala-azar has fever, massive splenomegaly, hepatomegaly, and pancytopenia.'),
('28151d49-cf37-5cf5-9ff2-3e7ac567f573'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which stain is used for Leishmania diagnosis?', '["Gram stain","Giemsa stain","Ziehl-Neelsen","India ink","PAS stain"]'::jsonb, 'Giemsa stain', 'Giemsa stain shows amastigotes (LD bodies) in bone marrow or splenic aspirate.'),
('195f45f3-5519-5714-835f-ed4cc2689ceb'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The treatment for visceral leishmaniasis is:', '["Chloroquine","Sodium stibogluconate","Metronidazole","Albendazole","Praziquantel"]'::jsonb, 'Sodium stibogluconate', 'Sodium stibogluconate (pentavalent antimonial) is the first-line drug for visceral leishmaniasis.'),
('f79a6466-4261-59b4-9ca2-1dc82443158e'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Giardia lamblia causes:', '["Liver abscess","Bloody diarrhea","Greasy, foul-smelling stools","Perianal itching","Hematuria"]'::jsonb, 'Greasy, foul-smelling stools', 'Giardia causes malabsorption with greasy, foul-smelling stools, bloating, and weight loss.'),
('01037a34-d136-54c5-929b-9bda6396df04'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The diagnostic stage of Giardia is:', '["Egg","Microfilaria","Cyst and trophozoite","Oocyst","Sporozoite"]'::jsonb, 'Cyst and trophozoite', 'Giardia diagnosis is by finding cysts (formed stool) or trophozoites (diarrheal stool).'),
('c7e7007a-291d-5546-b8af-5b12cf0f88ac'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Trichomonas vaginalis causes:', '["Bloody diarrhea clinical presentation","Lymphadenitis clinical presentation","Vaginitis with frothy discharge","Liver abscess clinical presentation","Steatorrhea clinical presentation"]'::jsonb, 'Vaginitis with frothy discharge', 'T. vaginalis causes vaginitis with frothy, yellow-green discharge and strawberry cervix.'),
('7720886e-c0d2-5ebc-a188-013a98064d00'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Trichomonas vaginalis is diagnosed by:', '["Wet mount microscopy","Blood smear","Stool culture","Urine culture","Serology"]'::jsonb, 'Wet mount microscopy', 'Wet mount of vaginal discharge shows motile flagellated trophozoites of T. vaginalis.'),
('89e96866-6a17-5812-b5ec-7422f194373b'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Schistosoma haematobium causes:', '["Pulmonary hypertension","Dermatitis","Intestinal schistosomiasis","Urinary schistosomiasis","Hepatosplenic schistosomiasis"]'::jsonb, 'Urinary schistosomiasis', 'S. haematobium affects the urinary bladder (terminal hematuria) and can cause bladder cancer.'),
('38ba6b4e-936f-5baf-b2f7-be97d3aec714'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The intermediate host for Schistosoma is:', '["Cow","Pig","Fish","Snail","Dog"]'::jsonb, 'Snail', 'Freshwater snails are the intermediate hosts for Schistosoma species.'),
('7f8f41b4-ab8a-568e-a663-de6b3a6ce756'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The infective stage of Schistosoma is:', '["Adult worm","Egg","Sporocyst","Miracidium","Cercaria"]'::jsonb, 'Cercaria', 'Cercariae penetrate human skin during contact with contaminated water.'),
('69939620-7b47-5930-8bee-efb5349e6f1b'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Diagnosis of schistosomiasis is confirmed by:', '["Eggs in stool or urine","Blood culture","Serology","X-ray","CT scan"]'::jsonb, 'Eggs in stool or urine', 'S. haematobium eggs are found in urine; S. mansoni eggs in stool.'),
('7d5420a9-2823-522f-a030-16a18aa2d5d6'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The treatment for all Schistosoma species is:', '["Ivermectin","Albendazole","DEC","Praziquantel","Metronidazole"]'::jsonb, 'Praziquantel', 'Praziquantel is effective against all Schistosoma species.'),
('54e0f2fc-4593-55ab-b62e-3590a82a166c'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Toxoplasma gondii causes:', '["Congenital toxoplasmosis","Malaria","Diarrhea","Liver abscess","Elephantiasis"]'::jsonb, 'Congenital toxoplasmosis', 'Toxoplasma causes congenital infection with classic triad: chorioretinitis, hydrocephalus, intracranial calcifications.'),
('a2efd21b-b499-5376-b828-520585480c81'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The definitive host for Toxoplasma gondii is:', '["Human","Dog","Sheep","Cat","Rat"]'::jsonb, 'Cat', 'Cats are the definitive host for T. gondii, excreting oocysts in feces.'),
('5a3d5059-6515-5172-bd52-eeee5508d1d8'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which drug is used for toxoplasmosis in pregnancy?', '["Metronidazole","Spiramycin","Pyrimethamine-sulfadiazine","Albendazole","Praziquantel"]'::jsonb, 'Spiramycin', 'Spiramycin is used in pregnancy to reduce transmission. Pyrimethamine-sulfadiazine is used after birth.'),
('ddf1bc80-ad41-5d3b-aa23-ae63286d2b49'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Plasmodium vivax causes which fever pattern?', '["Quartan fever","Irregular fever","Tertian fever","Continuous fever","Relapsing fever"]'::jsonb, 'Tertian fever', 'P. vivax causes tertian fever with paroxysms every 48 hours.'),
('9783ffc3-9105-5252-8f8d-f38c6c5a3602'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Plasmodium malariae causes which fever pattern?', '["Tertian fever","Quartan fever","Daily fever","Continuous fever","Irregular fever"]'::jsonb, 'Quartan fever', 'P. malariae causes quartan fever with paroxysms every 72 hours.'),
('c0085b7c-1934-535c-8b08-54f19a373d79'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The ''ring form'' is the diagnostic stage of which parasite in blood?', '["Wuchereria","Leishmania","Plasmodium","Trypanosoma","Babesia"]'::jsonb, 'Plasmodium', 'Ring stage (early trophozoite) of Plasmodium in RBCs is diagnostic for malaria.'),
('5d0dcbe7-e526-56ad-9654-ad4a161a6b11'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organ is most commonly affected by hydatid disease?', '["Spleen","Lung","Brain","Liver","Kidney"]'::jsonb, 'Liver', 'The liver is the most common site (60-70%) of hydatid cysts, followed by the lungs.'),
('ef0c2404-f6fb-59c0-bba4-ecb192b40c64'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Rupture of hydatid cyst can cause:', '["Obstruction","Infection","Bleeding","All of the above","Anaphylactic shock"]'::jsonb, 'Anaphylactic shock', 'Rupture of a hydatid cyst can cause anaphylaxis due to spillage of antigenic cyst fluid.'),
('6c76fb5a-8773-58d0-ba66-ee20fb4d8d71'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which nematode causes ''creeping eruption'' (cutaneous larva migrans)?', '["Hookworm of dogs/cats","Ascaris","Enterobius","Trichuris","Strongyloides"]'::jsonb, 'Hookworm of dogs/cats', 'Cutaneous larva migrans is caused by animal hookworm larvae (Ancylostoma caninum/braziliense).'),
('4368b7f6-31d1-58dd-a1c9-6cf28fff4c17'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which mosquito-borne viral infection has re-emerged in Pakistan?', '["Dengue fever","Japanese encephalitis","Yellow fever","West Nile fever","Chikungunya"]'::jsonb, 'Dengue fever', 'Dengue fever has caused major outbreaks in Pakistan since 2011, with all four serotypes circulating.'),
('f5c904c5-8a9e-5e9d-9485-c60b77ea19dc'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which parasite causes ''ocular toxocariasis''?', '["Wuchereria bancrofti","Toxocara canis","Ascaris lumbricoides","T. gondii","Onchocerca volvulus"]'::jsonb, 'Toxocara canis', 'Toxocara canis (dog roundworm) causes visceral and ocular larva migrans in humans.'),
('59284130-3b8c-5e9c-99e2-9aacbc88779c'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which is the drug of choice for neurocysticercosis?', '["Albendazole plus corticosteroids","Chloroquine","Ivermectin","Metronidazole","Praziquantel alone"]'::jsonb, 'Albendazole plus corticosteroids', 'Albendazole with corticosteroids is used for neurocysticercosis to reduce inflammation from dying cysts.'),
('a8564c11-d9fc-568f-9e61-83e098f60e47'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which protozoan causes ''primary amebic meningoencephalitis''?', '["Acanthamoeba species","Entamoeba histolytica","Trichomonas vaginalis","Naegleria fowleri","Giardia lamblia"]'::jsonb, 'Naegleria fowleri', 'Naegleria fowleri causes rapid fatal primary amebic meningoencephalitis in freshwater swimmers.'),
('df4a43c8-4293-5654-b625-7e7947bc7978'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''Acute hemorrhagic conjunctivitis''?', '["Enterovirus 70","HSV","Adenovirus","Chlamydia trachomatis","Coxsackievirus"]'::jsonb, 'Enterovirus 70', 'Enterovirus 70 causes acute hemorrhagic conjunctivitis, often in epidemics.'),
('4d6f4bda-6623-57f6-8e4e-f2dc99753f22'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which parasite causes ''scabies''?', '["Sarcoptes scabiei","Pediculus humanus","Tunga penetrans","Demodex folliculorum","Phthirus pubis"]'::jsonb, 'Sarcoptes scabiei', 'Sarcoptes scabiei (itch mite) burrows into the skin causing intense pruritus.'),
('78f964e3-7033-5e0b-910a-52cf71150c7e'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Myiasis is caused by:', '["Fleas","Lice","Ticks","Fly larvae","Mites"]'::jsonb, 'Fly larvae', 'Myiasis is infestation of living tissue by fly larvae (maggots).'),
('5b79ff20-8020-5c34-afae-440639a5f34e'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which mosquito-borne infection is caused by a filarial worm?', '["Dengue","Malaria","Yellow fever","Chikungunya","Lymphatic filariasis"]'::jsonb, 'Lymphatic filariasis', 'Wuchereria bancrofti and Brugia malayi cause lymphatic filariasis transmitted by mosquitoes.'),
('4d6c5645-c773-523c-b23e-8b142abc0c0d'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which hepatitis virus can also be transmitted via the fecal-oral route?', '["HAV","HBV","HGV","HDV","HCV"]'::jsonb, 'HAV', 'HAV (and HEV) are transmitted via the fecal-oral route, unlike HBV/HCV (blood-borne).'),
('bb3bee3c-cea9-5ba5-a2a7-a925ac57f8fd'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which vaccine is recommended for post-exposure prophylaxis of rabies?', '["Rabies vaccine + Rabies immunoglobulin","Tetanus vaccine clinical presentation","Immunoglobulin only clinical presentation","Rabies vaccine alone clinical presentation","No vaccine needed clinical presentation"]'::jsonb, 'Rabies vaccine + Rabies immunoglobulin', 'Post-exposure prophylaxis includes wound care, rabies vaccine (days 0,3,7,14,28), and RIG.'),
('d60f34ed-af79-5627-9dd4-5afe5e8e83ea'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which parasite causes ''kala-azar'' in Pakistan?', '["Leishmania tropica","Leishmania mexicana","Leishmania donovani","Leishmania major","Leishmania aethiopica"]'::jsonb, 'Leishmania donovani', 'Visceral leishmaniasis (Kala-azar) in Pakistan is caused by L. donovani.'),
('e1b70e4d-ad06-506e-bbaa-5cb5b6262ea3'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which is the most common intestinal protozoan in Pakistan?', '["Giardia lamblia","Cryptosporidium parvum","Entamoeba histolytica","Isospora belli","Cyclospora cayetanensis"]'::jsonb, 'Giardia lamblia', 'Giardia lamblia is the most commonly identified intestinal protozoan in Pakistan.'),
('40a5be8e-05dc-59db-b1c9-12fc10d8aaf0'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which test detects ''HBsAg''?', '["Serological ELISA","PCR","Blood culture","Urine antigen test","Stool antigen test"]'::jsonb, 'Serological ELISA', 'HBsAg is detected by serological ELISA (enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay).'),
('2bd388d2-ce3a-540d-ad1c-d8e489b9fd32'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism is most commonly isolated from patients with ''chronic suppurative otitis media''?', '["S. pneumoniae","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","E. coli","S. aureus","H. influenzae"]'::jsonb, 'Pseudomonas aeruginosa', 'Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a common isolate in chronic suppurative otitis media.'),
('90549eb8-3b37-5425-8927-3f1104b39165'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which serological test is used for syphilis screening?', '["TPHA","FTA-ABS","VDRL","ELISA","Western blot"]'::jsonb, 'VDRL', 'VDRL (Venereal Disease Research Laboratory) test is a non-treponemal screening test for syphilis.'),
('ccc2d7f6-294d-58ac-b948-cf0dabedcd91'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''brucellosis''?', '["Bacillus anthracis","Francisella tularensis","Pasteurella multocida","Brucella abortus","Yersinia pestis"]'::jsonb, 'Brucella abortus', 'Brucella abortus (cattle) causes brucellosis (undulant fever) with flu-like symptoms.'),
('e1bf09e4-e63a-5d9c-a4dc-73808f261248'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The ''Mantoux test'' is used for:', '["Diagnosis of syphilis","Screening for TB exposure","Diagnosis of HIV","Diagnosis of active TB","Diagnosis of leprosy"]'::jsonb, 'Screening for TB exposure', 'Mantoux test (PPD) screens for TB exposure/infection, but cannot distinguish active from latent TB.'),
('be833f8b-c983-53aa-b56d-b3034d948bb3'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''anthrax''?', '["Yersinia pestis","Bacillus cereus","Clostridium perfringens","Bacillus anthracis","Francisella tularensis"]'::jsonb, 'Bacillus anthracis', 'B. anthracis causes anthrax with characteristic eschar (malignant pustule).'),
('b39bf97d-3652-5690-989a-c2ae71c4d7e1'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria causes ''plague''?', '["Yersinia pestis","Pasteurella multocida","Yersinia enterocolitica","Francisella tularensis","Yersinia pseudotuberculosis"]'::jsonb, 'Yersinia pestis', 'Y. pestis causes plague (bubonic, pneumonic, septicemic), transmitted by rat fleas.'),
('4d97e930-d8b7-56d2-88a9-91c17ad5667e'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''trachoma''?', '["Haemophilus aegyptius","Moraxella lacunata","Chlamydia trachomatis","Adenovirus","Neisseria gonorrhoeae"]'::jsonb, 'Chlamydia trachomatis', 'Trachoma caused by C. trachomatis is the leading infectious cause of blindness worldwide.'),
('165f05b3-2bb9-5c80-9f02-f8a0abf88773'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which nematode causes ''elephantiasis''?', '["Wuchereria bancrofti","Dracunculus medinensis","Brugia malayi","Loa loa","Onchocerca volvulus"]'::jsonb, 'Wuchereria bancrofti', 'W. bancrofti causes 90% of lymphatic filariasis cases with elephantiasis.'),
('b8a30182-dcac-5f80-bfa8-198974324551'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which drug is used for mass drug administration for lymphatic filariasis?', '["DEC and albendazole","Chloroquine","Metronidazole","Ivermectin alone","Praziquantel"]'::jsonb, 'DEC and albendazole', 'WHO recommends DEC plus albendazole for mass drug administration in LF elimination programs.'),
('921a1979-3316-5454-b8d7-7a467a902911'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''onchocerciasis'' (river blindness)?', '["Dracunculus medinensis","Wuchereria bancrofti","Loa loa","Brugia malayi","Onchocerca volvulus"]'::jsonb, 'Onchocerca volvulus', 'O. volvulus causes onchocerciasis with blindness and skin disease, transmitted by blackflies.'),
('3f0464b0-4d6c-5ffd-ad52-a5ada5d6f44c'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'For a patient presenting with symptoms, Ivermectin is the drug of choice for:', '["Onchocerciasis and strongyloidiasis","Lymphatic filariasis","Schistosomiasis","Leishmaniasis","Malaria"]'::jsonb, 'Onchocerciasis and strongyloidiasis', 'Ivermectin is used for onchocerciasis, strongyloidiasis, and scabies.'),
('75048564-21cb-510f-9300-40ebaa375e2b'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''guineaworm disease''?', '["Onchocerca volvulus","Dracunculus medinensis","Wuchereria bancrofti","Loa loa","Trichinella spiralis"]'::jsonb, 'Dracunculus medinensis', 'D. medinensis (guineaworm) causes chronic ulcers when adult worms emerge through the skin.'),
('19badec3-272c-521d-b933-bd2803f698a3'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which parasite causes ''trichinosis''?', '["Trichuris trichiura","Toxoplasma gondii","Trichinella spiralis","Trichomonas vaginalis","Trypanosoma cruzi"]'::jsonb, 'Trichinella spiralis', 'Trichinosis is acquired by eating undercooked pork containing Trichinella cysts.'),
('f96d8058-bb08-5baf-928f-7c34eb375edc'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''toxocariasis''?', '["Enterobius vermicularis","Ascaris lumbricoides","Toxoplasma gondii","Toxocara canis/cati","Strongyloides stercoralis"]'::jsonb, 'Toxocara canis/cati', 'Toxocariasis (visceral larva migrans) is caused by dog and cat roundworms.'),
('cc6789d9-eec7-56c7-a30f-9899abec6587'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''cutaneous leishmaniasis'' in Pakistan?', '["Leishmania major","Leishmania brasiliensis","Leishmania infantum","Leishmania donovani","Leishmania tropica"]'::jsonb, 'Leishmania tropica', 'Cutaneous leishmaniasis in Pakistan is caused by L. tropica and L. major.'),
('ced58aa9-da91-5e28-ae3c-9ece7c8dd351'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The ''casoni test'' was used for diagnosis of:', '["Tuberculosis","Hydatid disease","Amebiasis","Leishmaniasis","Schistosomiasis"]'::jsonb, 'Hydatid disease', 'Casoni test (intradermal) was historically used for hydatid disease but is now replaced by serology.'),
('709bd5a1-ff64-5aee-b7ae-2ccf9d6f8ceb'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which gene/environmental condition predisposes to strongyloides hyperinfection?', '["Pregnancy","Genetic deficiency","Malnutrition","Immunosuppression","Young age"]'::jsonb, 'Immunosuppression', 'Immunosuppression, especially corticosteroids and HTLV-1 infection, predisposes to Strongyloides hyperinfection.'),
('04d8c21d-dac7-5b4e-853b-da74262d89d8'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which parasite causes ''sleeping sickness''?', '["Leishmania donovani","Trypanosoma brucei","Plasmodium falciparum","Trypanosoma cruzi","Toxoplasma gondii"]'::jsonb, 'Trypanosoma brucei', 'Trypanosoma brucei (gambiense/rhodesiense) causes African sleeping sickness.'),
('c2035045-bec1-5b19-8cac-37d8324e7a68'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The vector for Trypanosoma brucei is:', '["Blackfly","Tsetse fly","Sandfly","Reduviid bug","Mosquito"]'::jsonb, 'Tsetse fly', 'Tsetse fly (Glossina) transmits T. brucei.'),
('12d418e4-4f5c-5499-8aad-9366e66c2c56'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which parasite causes ''Chagas disease''?', '["Trypanosoma brucei","Plasmodium vivax","Toxoplasma gondii","Trypanosoma cruzi","Leishmania donovani"]'::jsonb, 'Trypanosoma cruzi', 'T. cruzi causes Chagas disease (American trypanosomiasis) with cardiomyopathy and megacolon.'),
('54eb3873-206b-5686-a38f-76250aa58532'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'The vector for Chagas disease is:', '["Mosquito","Sandfly","Reduviid (kissing) bug","Tsetse fly","Blackfly"]'::jsonb, 'Reduviid (kissing) bug', 'Reduviid bugs transmit T. cruzi. They defecate while feeding; the parasite enters through the wound.'),
('e2c099de-e4ab-5067-926a-d611c579b95b'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''cryptosporidiosis''?', '["Cryptosporidium parvum","Giardia lamblia","Cryptococcus neoformans","Isospora belli","Cyclospora cayetanensis"]'::jsonb, 'Cryptosporidium parvum', 'Cryptosporidium causes self-limiting diarrhea in immunocompetent but severe in AIDS patients.'),
('a7ea0038-e42b-5dd1-b0fa-a9fefcea497e'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which stain is used to detect Cryptosporidium?', '["Gram stain","Silver stain","Modified acid-fast stain","India ink","Giemsa stain"]'::jsonb, 'Modified acid-fast stain', 'Cryptosporidium oocysts are detected by modified Ziehl-Neelsen (acid-fast) stain.'),
('ecc6371a-aa2c-50ae-9377-8f62405e363d'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''cyclosporiasis''?', '["Isospora belli","Cryptosporidium parvum","Cyclospora cayetanensis","Toxoplasma gondii","Sarcocystis species"]'::jsonb, 'Cyclospora cayetanensis', 'Cyclospora cayetanensis causes prolonged watery diarrhea, associated with imported fresh produce.'),
('040ce3d1-4c5f-558e-9f7d-2807051263ef'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which food is commonly associated with Cyclospora outbreaks?', '["Imported raspberries/basil","Raw shellfish","Canned fish","Unpasteurized milk","Undercooked pork"]'::jsonb, 'Imported raspberries/basil', 'Cyclospora outbreaks have been linked to imported raspberries, basil, and lettuce.'),
('7ed188d6-93a7-5ec6-a248-3c84c9858088'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which tapeworm can cause ''sparganosis''?', '["Taenia saginata","Taenia solium","Spirometra species","Diphyllobothrium latum","Hymenolepis nana"]'::jsonb, 'Spirometra species', 'Sparganosis is caused by the larval stage of Spirometra tapeworms.'),
('b80951a9-5747-564b-bec2-9f4474cbac72'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which tapeworm causes ''vitamin B12 deficiency anemia''?', '["Taenia saginata","Hymenolepis nana","Taenia solium","Echinococcus granulosus","Diphyllobothrium latum"]'::jsonb, 'Diphyllobothrium latum', 'D. latum competes for vitamin B12, causing megaloblastic anemia.'),
('8c768cb2-66da-5065-a281-c1d5cdfb7548'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which is the smallest tapeworm infecting humans?', '["Echinococcus granulosus","Hymenolepis nana","Diphyllobothrium latum","Taenia solium","Taenia saginata"]'::jsonb, 'Hymenolepis nana', 'H. nana (dwarf tapeworm) is the smallest tapeworm, causing self-limited infection.'),
('e6043a8b-66e1-5b1a-8db0-967a08c431be'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''babesiosis''?', '["Babesia microti","Leishmania donovani","Trypanosoma cruzi","Toxoplasma gondii","Plasmodium falciparum"]'::jsonb, 'Babesia microti', 'Babesiosis is a tick-borne hemoprotozoan disease causing hemolytic anemia.'),
('ae712070-6834-5ea4-9db6-ee77961b37a7'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''gnathostomiasis''?', '["Gnathostoma spinigerum","Onchocerca volvulus","Wuchereria bancrofti","Strongyloides stercoralis","Ancylostoma duodenale"]'::jsonb, 'Gnathostoma spinigerum', 'Gnathostomiasis causes migratory subcutaneous swellings, acquired by eating undercooked freshwater fish.'),
('d99b24a4-8904-5e95-ad4d-addc47876bfb'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''angiostrongyliasis''?', '["Necator americanus","Strongyloides stercoralis","Trichostrongylus orientalis","Angiostrongylus cantonensis","Ancylostoma caninum"]'::jsonb, 'Angiostrongylus cantonensis', 'A. cantonensis causes eosinophilic meningitis, acquired by eating infected snails/slugs.'),
('c49590df-86f2-5ed1-9e62-c1b4ea05ad61'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which drug is used for mass treatment of scabies in communities?', '["Permethrin 5% cream","Ivermectin oral","Gamma benzene hexachloride","Crotamiton","Sulfur ointment"]'::jsonb, 'Ivermectin oral', 'Oral ivermectin is effective for mass drug administration for scabies.'),
('c9c671b8-ff45-5a20-b19c-e79afef7687d'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''pediculosis capitis''?', '["Pediculus humanus corporis","Pediculus humanus capitis","Phthirus pubis","Sarcoptes scabiei","Demodex folliculorum"]'::jsonb, 'Pediculus humanus capitis', 'Head lice (Pediculus humanus capitis) infest the scalp causing pruritus.'),
('a7dd1e68-d785-5521-b9b0-4c527853cacd'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''tungiasis''?', '["Tunga penetrans","Sarcoptes scabiei","Xenopsylla cheopis","Pulex irritans","Ctenocephalides felis"]'::jsonb, 'Tunga penetrans', 'Tunga penetrans (jigger flea) burrows into the skin, usually on the feet.'),
('8c37ab86-5f9e-58de-a271-a7e2ebb4da74'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria is the most common cause of peritonitis in cirrhotic patients?', '["Escherichia coli","Staphylococcus aureus","Bacteroides fragilis","Streptococcus pneumoniae","Klebsiella pneumoniae"]'::jsonb, 'Escherichia coli', 'E. coli is the most common cause of spontaneous bacterial peritonitis in cirrhotic patients with ascites.'),
('a84e2d3d-d6c6-5a41-8609-f914abc8e408'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism is most commonly responsible for ''catheter-related bloodstream infections''?', '["Staphylococcus epidermidis","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Candida albicans","Staphylococcus aureus","Escherichia coli"]'::jsonb, 'Staphylococcus epidermidis', 'Coagulase-negative staphylococci (especially S. epidermidis) are the most common cause of catheter-related bloodstream infections.'),
('316fc0dc-9515-5cf7-b294-416dcfef6481'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which is the most common cause of ''infective endocarditis'' overall?', '["Staphylococcus aureus","Streptococcus viridans","Enterococcus faecalis","Streptococcus bovis","Staphylococcus epidermidis"]'::jsonb, 'Streptococcus viridans', 'S. viridans (oral streptococci) is historically the most common cause of native valve endocarditis.'),
('fd31b83d-f39a-573b-bc14-257af23a478f'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism is associated with ''Whipple disease''?', '["Mycobacterium avium","Yersinia enterocolitica","Campylobacter jejuni","Tropheryma whipplei","Helicobacter pylori"]'::jsonb, 'Tropheryma whipplei', 'Tropheryma whipplei causes Whipple disease with malabsorption, arthritis, and CNS involvement.'),
('8eadd304-b7fe-5a44-870e-4df632a58ee2'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria causes ''Listeriosis'' in pregnancy?', '["Listeria monocytogenes","Streptococcus agalactiae","Escherichia coli","Staphylococcus aureus","Clostridium perfringens"]'::jsonb, 'Listeria monocytogenes', 'Listeria monocytogenes causes listeriosis with flu-like illness in pregnancy and severe neonatal infection.'),
('6c9ae094-a5cd-51ec-8d18-6ac89565e236'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''tropical pyomyositis''?', '["Streptococcus pyogenes","Escherichia coli","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Staphylococcus aureus","Clostridium perfringens"]'::jsonb, 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'S. aureus is the most common cause of tropical pyomyositis (muscle abscesses).'),
('19f1e2aa-39c1-5b09-a572-28d0b2359a6e'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which organism causes ''Chancroid''?', '["Chlamydia trachomatis","Treponema pallidum","Calymmatobacterium granulomatis","Neisseria gonorrhoeae","Haemophilus ducreyi"]'::jsonb, 'Haemophilus ducreyi', 'H. ducreyi causes chancroid with painful genital ulcers and inguinal lymphadenopathy.'),
('6d5c6289-f46d-5b67-a320-fbd0b8725287'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria causes ''granuloma inguinale'' (donovanosis)?', '["Chlamydia trachomatis","Neisseria gonorrhoeae","Treponema pallidum","Klebsiella granulomatis","Haemophilus ducreyi"]'::jsonb, 'Klebsiella granulomatis', 'Donovanosis is caused by K. granulomatis (formerly Calymmatobacterium granulomatis).'),
('dd0833eb-6ee4-5533-972e-86fab8db9eda'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria produces ''toxic shock syndrome toxin-1'' (TSST-1)?', '["Streptococcus pyogenes","Staphylococcus aureus","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Clostridium difficile","Escherichia coli"]'::jsonb, 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'S. aureus produces TSST-1, causing toxic shock syndrome with fever, hypotension, and rash.'),
('0fd02bdd-b380-5a9d-a872-567389ac7190'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria produces ''Streptococcal pyrogenic exotoxins''?', '["Streptococcus pyogenes","Streptococcus pneumoniae","Streptococcus agalactiae","Staphylococcus aureus","Enterococcus faecalis"]'::jsonb, 'Streptococcus pyogenes', 'S. pyogenes produces streptococcal pyrogenic exotoxins (Spe) causing scarlet fever and toxic shock-like syndrome.'),
('4c00f330-f048-56a6-ad1e-d5e05a4b53c2'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria is associated with ''Reactive arthritis'' after GI infection?', '["Campylobacter jejuni","Escherichia coli","Staphylococcus aureus","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Bacteroides fragilis"]'::jsonb, 'Campylobacter jejuni', 'Campylobacter, Salmonella, Shigella, and Yersinia can trigger reactive arthritis.'),
('01873dc7-bcdd-53f7-844e-74028c2053c4'::uuid, 'Pathology (Paper 1)', 'Microbiology', 'Which bacteria is the most common cause of ''community-acquired pneumonia''?', '["Chlamydia pneumoniae","Haemophilus influenzae","Legionella pneumophila","Mycoplasma pneumoniae","Streptococcus pneumoniae"]'::jsonb, 'Streptococcus pneumoniae', 'S. pneumoniae is the most common cause of community-acquired pneumonia.');
